$WW,1$$FG,5,1$ZealOS Filesystem Tools$FG$

$FG,2$Overview$FG$

This directory contains filesystem utilities for creating, checking,
and inspecting filesystems from within ZealOS.

$FG,2$Available Tools$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,3$Formatting Tools (mkfs)$FG$

  $FG,4$MkfsExt4(device, opts)$FG$
    Create an ext4 filesystem on a device.
    - 64-bit block addressing support
    - Extent trees
    - Directory hashing (htree)
    - Journal support

  $FG,4$MkfsExt3(device, opts)$FG$
    Create an ext3 filesystem (ext4 without extents).

  $FG,4$MkfsExt2(device, opts)$FG$
    Create an ext2 filesystem (no journal).

  $FG,4$MkfsFat32(device, opts)$FG$
    Create a FAT32 filesystem.
    - Auto cluster size selection
    - Volume label support

$FG,3$Checking Tools (fsck)$FG$

  $FG,4$FsckExt4(device, flags)$FG$
    Check and repair ext2/3/4 filesystems.
    - Pass 1: Inode checking
    - Pass 2: Directory structure
    - Pass 3: Reference counts
    - Pass 4: Block bitmaps

  $FG,4$FsckFat32(device, flags)$FG$
    Check FAT32 filesystems.
    - FAT table comparison
    - Directory structure validation
    - Lost cluster detection

$FG,3$Information Tools$FG$

  $FG,4$DumpExt4Info(device)$FG$
    Display ext2/3/4 superblock and group descriptor info.
    Similar to Linux dumpe2fs.

  $FG,4$DumpNtfsInfo(device)$FG$
    Display NTFS volume information.
    - Boot sector details
    - MFT records
    - Volume name and version

  $FG,4$DumpFat32Info(device)$FG$
    Display FAT32 volume information.
    - Boot sector details
    - FSInfo data
    - Free space$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Flags$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,4$FSCK Flags:$FG$
  FSCK_READONLY  (0x0001) - Don't modify filesystem
  FSCK_VERBOSE   (0x0002) - Verbose output
  FSCK_FORCE     (0x0004) - Force check even if clean$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Usage$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,3$Load all tools:$FG$
  #include "/Home/POSIX/vfs/tools/MakeFSTools.ZC"

$FG,3$Format a partition:$FG$
  // Create ext4 with defaults
  MkfsExt4("/dev/sda1", NULL);

  // Create ext4 with options
  CMkfsExt4Opts opts;
  MkfsExt4DefaultOpts(&opts);
  opts.label = "MYVOLUME";
  opts.block_size = 4096;
  MkfsExt4("/dev/sda1", &opts);

$FG,3$Check a filesystem:$FG$
  // Read-only verbose check
  FsckExt4("/dev/sda1", FSCK_READONLY | FSCK_VERBOSE);

  // Force check
  FsckExt4("/dev/sda1", FSCK_FORCE);

$FG,3$View filesystem info:$FG$
  DumpExt4Info("/dev/sda1");
  DumpNtfsInfo("/dev/sdb1");
  DumpFat32Info("/dev/sdc1");$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Return Values$FG$

$ID,2$FSCK_OK          (0)  - No errors found
FSCK_CORRECTED   (1)  - Errors were corrected
FSCK_REBOOT      (2)  - System should be rebooted
FSCK_ERRORS      (4)  - Errors remain uncorrected
FSCK_OPERATIONAL (8)  - Operational error (can't open device)$ID,-2$

$FG,2$License$FG$

$ID,2$MIT License

These tools are clean-room implementations based on publicly
available filesystem specifications.$ID,-2$

